        "original_id": "9e13292f-c642-52a7-87a6-98b18143d30e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Desaga, Robert Wilhelm Bunsen, Michael Faraday\n- Organizations: University of Heidelberg\n- Products: Bunsen burner, laboratory burner\n- Topics: instrument making, electromagnetism, electrochemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Faraday was born on 22 September 1791 and died on 25 August 1867.\n- Michael Faraday was an English scientist who contributed to the study of electromagnetism and electrochemistry.\n- Peter Desaga was a German instrument maker at the University of Heidelberg who worked with Robert Wilhelm Bunsen.\n- In 1855, Peter Desaga perfected Michael Faraday's earlier laboratory burner design into the Bunsen burner.",
